 submit a strategy for cyber cooperation in the Indo-Pacific region, and for other purposes.","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5211"},{"title":"A bill to require a drone posture review.","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5340"},{"title":"Military Leadership Removal Transparency Act of 2026","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5343"},{"title":"A bill to provide for the delivery of artificial intelligence functional bills of materials, and for other purposes.","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5345"},{"title":"Responsible Artificial Intelligence Defense Act of 2026","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/4707"},{"title":"ARCH Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5375"},{"title":"A bill to require the Secretary of Defense to establish a pilot program on Department of Defense partnerships with institutions of higher education recognized in the National Centers of Academic Excellence in Cybersecurity program for Cyber Research, and for other purposes.","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5504"},{"title":"Blocking Foreign Cellular Modules in Defense Systems Act of 2026","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5598"},{"title":"Insider Threat Reporting and Security Guidance Act of 2026","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5601"},{"title":"Military Domestic Violence Survivors Support Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/10870"},{"title":"Electric Grid Supply Chain Security Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5590"},{"title":"Military DEI Repeal Act of 2026","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5596"},{"title":"Weapons Resupply, Stockpile, and Assurance Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5595"},{"title":"River Ridge Land Conveyance Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5599"},{"title":"Service Academy Testing Enhancement Act of 2026","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/5597"}],"textVersions":[{"date":"2026-06-15","stage":"Reported to Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119s4784rs/xml/BILLS-119s4784rs.xml"}],"summaries":[{"date":"2026-06-15","stage":"Reported to Senate","text":"National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2027\n\nThis bill sets forth policies and authorities for FY2027 for Department of Defense (DOD) programs, activities, and military construction as well as the national security programs of the Department of Energy (DOE).\n\nAmong other elements, the bill\n\nauthorizes the procurement of various items, including aircraft and ships;\nsets active duty and reserve component personnel strength levels;\nsets policy regarding various aspects of military health care and military compensation;\nsets policy regarding DOD acquisitions and acquisition management, including contracting authorities;\nsets policy for various matters related to DOD interactions with foreign nations, including matters concerning the Middle East, Europe, and the Indo-Pacific;\nsets policy for various matters related to DOD cyber operations, cyber forces, cybersecurity, and artificial intelligence;\nrequires DOD to review certain materials (including boron carbide, copper foil, and synthetic diamond) to determine actions to maintain access to critical defense industry components and materials, and report to Congress on such matters; \nauthorizes DOD's Office of Strategic Capital to make equity investments in non-federal entities with respect to batteries and critical minerals, materials, and chemicals;\nauthorizes specified military construction projects and extends the authorization of certain projects from previous fiscal years; and \nauthorizes the National Nuclear Security Administration and the Defense Nuclear Facilities Safety Board.\n\nFor additional information on the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA) see\n\nIn Focus IF10516, Defense Primer: Navigating the NDAA, and\nIn Focus IF10515, Defense Primer: The NDAA Process."}],"actions":[{"date":"2026-07-27","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure made in Senate. (CR S4276)"},{"date":"2026-07-23","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure withdrawn in Senate."},{"date":"2026-07-23","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure made in Senate. (CR S4241-4242)"},{"date":"2026-07-20","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure made in Senate. (CR S4145)"},{"date":"2026-07-14","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure made in Senate. (CR S3919)"},{"date":"2026-07-14","text":"Motion by Senator Thune to reconsider the vote by which cloture on the motion to proceed to the measure was not invoked (Record Vote No. 195) entered in Senate."},{"date":"2026-07-14","text":"Cloture motion on the motion to proceed to the measure not invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 50 - 46. Record Vote Number: 195. (CR S3918)"},{"date":"2026-06-24","text":"Cloture motion on the motion to proceed to the measure presented in Senate. (CR S3193)"},{"date":"2026-06-24","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure made in Senate. (CR S3193)"},{"date":"2026-06-15","text":"Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 436."},{"date":"2026-06-15","text":"Committee on Armed Services. Original measure reported to Senate by Senator Wicker. With written report No. 119-127."},{"date":"2026-06-15","text":"Committee on Armed Services. Original measure reported to Senate by Senator Wicker. With written report No. 119-127."}]},"votes":[{"chamber":"Senate","congress":119,"session":2,"roll":195,"date":"2026-07-14","time":"02:41 PM","question":"On Cloture on the Motion to Proceed S. 4784","description":"Motion to Invoke Cloture: Motion to Proceed to S. 4784","result":"Cloture on the Motion to Proceed Rejected (50-46, 3/5 majority required)","amendment":"","amendmentDetail":"","tieBreaker":"","url":"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00195.htm","xmlUrl":"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00195.xml","counts":{"yes":50,"no":46,"present":0,"notVoting":4},"members":[{"id":"S428","name":"Alsobrooks, Angela","state":"MD","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S440","name":"Armstrong, Alan","state":"OK","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":"S354","name":"Baldwin, Tammy","state":"WI","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S429","name":"Banks, Jim","state":"IN","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":"S317","name":"Barrasso, John","state":"WY","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":"S330","name":"Bennet, Michael","state":"CO","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S396","name":"Blackburn, Marsha","state":"TN","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":"S341","name":"Blumenthal, Richard","state":"CT","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S430","name":"Blunt Rochester, Lisa","state":"DE","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S370","name":"Booker, Cory","state":"NJ","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S343","name":"Boozman, John","state":"AR","party":"R","district":"","vote"